Classic IMPORT INTO same-target owner race, 2026-07-25

Environment
-----------
TiDB binary: v9.0.0-beta.2.pre-2017-ged2376acc6
Current source: 231dad5225f0d3c9cf38d4ab7ebc03a5326785c7
Relevant source diff between the two commits: empty
Topology: one TiDB, one PD, one real TiKV
MDL: ON
Target: t(v VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL, UNIQUE KEY uk(v)), hidden row handle
Inputs: disjoint aNNNNNNN and bNNNNNNN values
Fault injection or product modification: none

Default-config natural RED, 1,000,000 rows per input
----------------------------------------------------
Two ordinary MySQL clients submitted detached imports concurrently.

job 8:
  created 2026-07-25 05:27:42.817071
  started 2026-07-25 05:27:43.354266
  failed during validation with ErrChecksumMismatch
  remote total_kvs=3000000, local total_kvs=2000000

job 9:
  created 2026-07-25 05:27:42.817201
  started 2026-07-25 05:27:43.874099
  finished successfully with imported_rows=1000000

Durable state after both terminal results:
  record scan:       1000000 rows, A=0,       B=1000000
  unique-index scan: 2000000 rows, A=1000000, B=1000000
  lookup a0000001 through uk returned handle 1, value b0000001
  lookup b0000001 through uk returned handle 1, value b0000001
  ADMIN CHECK TABLE: error 8223

The same default-config RED occurred with 100,000 rows per input:
  both jobs were admitted
  one finished and one failed checksum
  record/index counts were 100000/200000
  the winner reversed between runs

A 100,000-row rate-limited run also produced the same RED shape. The
rate limit was used only to observe phases and is not required by the bug.

Matched controls
----------------
Sequential submission while the first job was running:
  second IMPORT INTO failed before admission with error 8258
  "Table t is in mode Import"
  first job finished
  record/index counts were 100000/100000
  ADMIN CHECK TABLE succeeded

One default 100,000-row concurrent run admitted both jobs, but DXF happened
to schedule them serially. The second job then failed precheck with
"target table is not empty", and record/index counts were 100000/100000.
This isolates the irreversible boundary: dual admission becomes corruption
when both accepted owners overlap physical ingest.

Source closure
--------------
GetActiveJobCnt and CreateJob do not form one atomic per-target claim.
Classic then relies on TableModeImport, but TableMode carries no owner ID and
CanTransitionTo explicitly allows Import -> Import. Two submissions that both
plan before the first schema change becomes visible can therefore both commit
the same mode and publish separate jobs. A later sequential submission is
blocked by optimizer error 8258, matching the control.

The standalone Lightning write-overlap probe produced the same physical
record/index corruption, but official product documentation states that
physical Lightning requires an empty target and no writes during import.
That result is retained only as a mechanism calibration, not as a new bug.
